## Scope
Skills are on-demand expertise. `name` must match the folder that contains `SKILL.md`.

## Three kinds
- **Lock-installed** — upstream catalogs in `scripts/skills-lock-manifest.mjs`; tree under `.agents/skills/` (gitignored). Folder names match upstream (`nextjs`, `shadcn`, `vercel-composition-patterns`).
- **Workflow** — Basilic playbooks at `.agents/skills/workflow/w-<name>/`. `disable-model-invocation: true`. One-line `description`.
- **Rules** — repo constraints in `.cursor/rules/` and `AGENTS.md` override skill examples (style, layout, stack).

## Principles
- One primary topic per skill; independent versions = separate upstream skills or rule files
- `name` lowercase/digits/hyphens, max 64, equals folder name
- Basilic playbook names start with `w-`
- Prefer `paths` over legacy `globs` when file-scoped
- Declarative: state what is true. Patterns over long examples
- Progressive disclosure: keep `SKILL.md` short; depth in `references/` or `PATTERNS.md`
- No repo-specific paths in upstream tech skills. Rules override skills
- Workflow descriptions stay one line (discovery tokens are always-on)

## Hierarchy
Rules (constraints) > skills (patterns) > model

Update procedure: `apps/docu/content/docs/development/cursor-skills.mdx`. `pnpm setup:skills` installs the manifest with `--agent cursor` only. Daily path: `/w-plan`, `/w-grill`, `/w-wayfinder`, `/w-build`, `/w-ship`.

Playbook bodies are numbered instructions (spec frontmatter); keep simple playbooks short. Git playbooks carry `references/git-publish.md`. `/w-plan` explores via `/w-council` first and ships `references/plan-output.md`. `/w-grill` ships `references/round-format.md`. `/w-wayfinder` ships `references/map-output.md`.
